@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- National Insurance Law [Consolidated Version], 5755-1995, row IL-33: the statuses s 335 reads, s 238,
-- residence (s 2A), ss 69, 69A and 71, and the surroundings of the child allowance.
-- THE NOUNS: DECLARE and nothing else. Every rules module of this row imports this one.
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/national-insurance-law-consolidated-version-5755-1995.he.wiki.txt,
-- Hebrew Wikisource raw MediaWiki, retrieved 2026-10-06, sha256 78bf47ee...552a97. An unofficial
-- consolidation of the text as amended at retrieval. A `src:N` comment quotes line N of that file,
-- generated by tools/srcquote.py; nothing in Hebrew here is typed by hand.
--
-- Membership test: a witness of ordinary competence could testify to the fact, or a register of the
-- Institute records it. Whether the fact makes a person insured, a resident or a housewife is a rule,
-- and belongs in the section module that says so.
--
-- A FACT THE LAW LEAVES TO ANOTHER TEXT is a field here, named for the text that decides it: the
-- regulations under ss 75 and 243, the Entry to Israel Law and Regulations,
-- the Security Service Law are not deposited. None of them is guessed. (The Retirement Age Law 5764-2004 is deposited and is read through row IL-27's module, vendored here.)

§ `Nouns for row IL-33 of the National Insurance Law`

§§ `The person`

-- s 1 "גיל הפרישה" and s 238 speak of a man and of a woman.
-- src:130 | ”גיל הפרישה“ –
-- src:131 | (1) לגבי גבר – הגיל הקבוע לו בהתאם לחודש לידתו בחלק א׳ בלוח א׳1;
-- src:132 | (2) לגבי אישה – הגיל הקבוע לה בהתאם לחודש לידתה לפי חלק א׳ בלוח א׳1, ואם היא נולדה בשנת 1956 ואילך – הגיל הקבוע לה בהתאם לחוק גיל פרישה, התשס״ד–2004;
DECLARE `Sex` IS ONE OF
    `male`
    `female`

-- s 2A(b) and (c): the permission under which a person stays in Israel, where the Entry to Israel
-- Law and Regulations are the text that gives it a name. Those instruments are not deposited, so the
-- types of visa are taken as the section names them. `no permission that section 2A names` is a
-- citizen, an oleh, or any stay none of its paragraphs reaches.
-- For the two visas whose paragraphs turn on how long the holder lived lawfully in Israel in "the
-- determining year" (the year that begins 183 days before the day the visa and licence were granted),
-- the count of those days is a fact the Institute holds; it is not computed here.
-- src:245 | (ב) לענין חוק זה לא יראו כתושב ישראל, בין השאר, כל אחד מאלה:
-- src:246 | (1) שוהה שלא כדין, כמשמעותו בסעיף 13 בחוק הכניסה לישראל;
-- src:247 | (2) מי שבידו היתר כאמור בצו הכניסה לישראל (פטור תושבי יהודה ושומרון, רצועת עזה וצפון סיני, מרכז סיני, מרחב שלמה ורמת הגולן), התשכ״ח–1968;
-- src:248 | (3) מי שבידו אשרה ורישיון לישיבת ביקור מסוג ב/1, ב/2, ב/3 או ב/4, לפי תקנה 5 בתקנות הכניסה;
-- src:249 | (3א) מי שבידו אשרה ורישיון לפי תקנה 5א לתקנות הכניסה;
-- src:250 | (4) מי שבידו אשרה ורישיון לישיבת ארעי מסוג א/1, לפי תקנה 6(א) בתקנות הכניסה – בתקופות שלהלן, לפי העניין:
-- src:251 | (א) בשנה שתחילתה 183 ימים לפני יום מתן האשרה והרישיון כאמור (בסעיף זה – השנה הקובעת) – אם התגורר כדין בישראל פחות מ־183 ימים באותה שנה;
-- src:252 | (ב) בתקופה שלפני יום מתן האשרה והרישיון כאמור – אם התגורר כדין בישראל בשנה הקובעת יותר מ־183 ימים;
-- src:253 | (5) מי שבידו אשרה ורישיון לישיבת ארעי מסוג א/3 לפי תקנה 6(ג) בתקנות הכניסה, וכן קרובו של בעל אשרה ורישיון כאמור שבידו אשרה ורישיון לישיבת ארעי מסוג א/4 לפי תקנה 6(ד) בתקנות הכניסה.
-- src:254 | (ג) מי שאינו אזרח ישראלי ובידו אשרה ורישיון לישיבה בישראל לפי חוק הכניסה לישראל שאינם מנויים בסעיף קטן (ב)(3) עד (5), לא יראו אותו כתושב ישראל בתקופות שלהלן, לפי העניין:
-- src:255 | (1) בשנה הקובעת – אם התגורר כדין בישראל פחות מ־183 ימים באותה שנה;
-- src:256 | (2) בתקופה שלפני יום מתן האשרה והרישיון כאמור – אם התגורר כדין בישראל בשנה הקובעת יותר מ־183 ימים.
-- src:257 | (ד) על אף הוראות סעיף קטן (ב)(4), מי שבידו אשרה ורישיון לישיבת ארעי כאמור באותו סעיף קטן, ניתנה לו אשרת עולה או תעודת עולה לפי חוק השבות, בתוך השנה שתחילתה ביום מתן האשרה והרישיון האמורים, רשאי המוסד לראות בו תושב ישראל מיום מתן האשרה והרישיון.
DECLARE `The permission under which a person stays in Israel` IS ONE OF
    `no permission that section 2A names`
    `unlawful presence within section 13 of the Entry to Israel Law`
    `a permit under the Entry to Israel Order (exemption of residents of Judea and Samaria, the Gaza Strip and northern Sinai, central Sinai, the Sharm el-Sheikh area and the Golan Heights), 5728-1968`
    `a visitor's visa and licence of type B/1, B/2, B/3 or B/4, under regulation 5 of the Entry Regulations`
    `a visa and licence under regulation 5A of the Entry Regulations`
    `a temporary-residence visa and licence of type A/1, under regulation 6(a) of the Entry Regulations` HAS
        `the day the visa and licence were granted`                                              IS A DATE
        `the days the holder lived lawfully in Israel in the determining year`                    IS A NUMBER
        `the Institute regards the holder as a resident from the day it was granted, section 2A(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a temporary-residence visa and licence of type A/3 (regulation 6(c)), or of type A/4 as a relative of the holder of A/3 (regulation 6(d)), of the Entry Regulations`
    `another visa and licence for residence under the Entry to Israel Law, held by a person who is not an Israeli citizen, which section 2A(c) reaches` HAS
        `the day the visa and licence were granted`                                              IS A DATE
        `the days the holder lived lawfully in Israel in the determining year`                    IS A NUMBER

-- The facts of residence on the day asked about.
-- `lives in Israel`: the Law gives no positive test of residence (no definition of "תושב ישראל" or
-- "יושב בישראל" in s 1; s 2A says only who is NOT a resident, "among others"), so whether the
-- person's life is in Israel is the one positive fact the case supplies (fork R1, NOTES.md).
-- `absent from Israel beyond a reasonable temporary absence`: the opinion of the Institute's employee
-- authorised for it (s 65(a) "מבוטח" (2)); a recorded determination, not decided here.
-- `the day the person first became an Israeli resident`: s 240(a) reads it; NOTHING if never.
-- `a temporary resident`: "תושב ארעי", s 158(1); the Law does not define the term (fork R2).
-- src:803 | (2) יחיד היושב בישראל, ואינו נעדר ממנה אלא העדר ארעי שהוא סביר, לדעת עובד המוסד שהוסמך לכך, ואין בו לסתור טענת אותו יחיד כי הוא יושב בישראל, ואינו מבוטח לפי פרק י״א, למעט עקרת בית כהגדרתה בסעיף 238;
-- src:1444 | (1) תושב ישראל או תושב ארעי שמלאו לו 18 שנים וטרם הגיע לגיל הקבוע לגביו, בהתאם לחודש לידתו, בחלק ב׳ בלוח א׳1, והוא עובד הזכאי לשכר שמעבידו חייב בתשלום דמי ביטוח בעדו;
DECLARE `The residence facts of a person` HAS
    `lives in Israel`                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `permission to stay`                                                      IS A `The permission under which a person stays in Israel`
    `absent from Israel beyond a reasonable temporary absence`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the person first became an Israeli resident`                     IS A MAYBE DATE
    `a temporary resident`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Work`

-- s 75(a)(3) to (8): the categories, beside employees and the self-employed, that Chapter 5 insures.
-- Each needs a fact (an approved place, a service the regulations call ordinary) that regulations
-- decide; the list says which categories the person is in.
-- src:947 | (3) אדם המצוי בהכשרה מקצועית או בשיקום מקצועי, במקום או אצל אדם שאושר לכך בתקנות;
-- src:948 | (4) אדם הנבחן לפי סעיף 22 לחוק החניכות, התשי״ג–1953, או לפי הפרק השלישי לחוק שירות התעסוקה, והוא בשעת הבחינה בלבד;
-- src:949 | (5) מי שמתאמן לפי חוק שירות עבודה בשעת חירום, התשכ״ז–1967;
-- src:950 | (6) אסיר או עציר העובד בעבודה שאינה מן השירותים שנקבעו בתקנות כשירותים רגילים של בית סוהר או של מקום מעצר;
-- src:951 | (7) חוסה במעון או במעון נעול על פי חוק הנוער, העובד בעבודה שאינה מן השירותים שנקבעו כשירותים רגילים של מעון או מעון נעול כאמור;
-- src:952 | (8) מי ששכרו נקבע על פי חוק.
DECLARE `A further category insured under section 75(a)` IS ONE OF
    `in vocational training or rehabilitation at a place or with a person approved in regulations, section 75(a)(3)`
    `being examined under section 22 of the Apprenticeship Law or Chapter 3 of the Employment Service Law, during the examination only, section 75(a)(4)`
    `training under the Emergency Work Service Law, 5727-1967, during the training, section 75(a)(5)`
    `a prisoner or detainee doing work other than the ordinary services of a prison or place of detention, section 75(a)(6)`
    `a ward of a hostel or locked hostel under the Youth Law doing work other than its ordinary services, section 75(a)(7)`
    `a person whose wage is fixed by law, section 75(a)(8)`

-- `an employee` and `a self-employed person`: s 1 "עובד" and "עובד עצמאי", which row IL-04 encodes;
-- the Institute records which a person is for the period. `entitled to wages on which the employer
-- must pay insurance contributions`: s 158 "מבוטח" (1).
-- `a police officer, a prison officer or a security-service employee`: the three the first paragraph of
-- s 75(a) leaves out. `of a class of self-employed persons the regulations exclude`: s 75(a)(2).
-- The facts about work abroad are s 76(a) and (b).
-- `a member of a collective or renewed kibbutz regarded as a worker under section 3 or 3A(a)`: s 158
-- "עובד" excludes such a member.
-- src:945 | (1) עובד, למעט שוטר כמשמעותו בחוק המשטרה, סוהר כמשמעותו בחוק שירות בתי הסוהר ועובד שירותי הבטחון כמשמעותו בסעיף 63א לחוק שירות המדינה;
-- src:946 | (2) עובד עצמאי, למעט מי שנמנה עם סוג אנשים שהוצאו מכלל עובדים עצמאיים, לענין סעיף זה, בתקנות ולאחר התייעצות עם ועדת העבודה והרווחה;
-- src:956 | (א) העובד בחוץ לארץ מבוטח לפי פרק זה אם הוא ומעבידו הם תושבי ישראל וחוזה העבודה נקשר בישראל, או אף אם חוזה העבודה לא נקשר בישראל ובמקום העבודה אין ביטוח נפגעי עבודה חובה לפי החוק ונמסרה הודעה על קיומו של החוזה כפי שנקבע בתקנות.
-- src:957 | (ב) על אף הוראות סעיף קטן (א), אם שהה העובד בחוץ לארץ, תקופה העולה על חמש שנים רצופות, לא יהיה מבוטח לפי פרק זה אם לא התיר השר או מי שהשר הסמיך לכך את ביטוחו בתקופת עבודתו בחוץ לארץ שלאחר חמש השנים.
-- src:1453 | ”עובד“ – למעט חבר אגודה שיתופית שהיא קיבוץ שיתופי או קיבוץ מתחדש, שרואים אותו כעובד לפי הוראות סעיף 3 או 3א(א);
DECLARE `The work facts of a person` HAS
    `an employee`                                                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `a self-employed person`                                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `a police officer, a prison officer or a security-service employee`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `of a class of self-employed persons the regulations exclude`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `further categories insured under section 75(a)`                                                IS A LIST OF `A further category insured under section 75(a)`
    `works outside Israel`                                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer is an Israeli resident`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract of employment was made in Israel`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `no compulsory work injury insurance applies at the place of work`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice of the contract of employment was given as the regulations prescribe`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `has stayed abroad for more than five consecutive years`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister or his delegate permitted the insurance after the five years`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `a controlling shareholder in a closely-held company`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `a member of a collective or renewed kibbutz regarded as a worker under section 3 or 3A(a)`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `entitled to wages on which the employer must pay insurance contributions`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `was insured as an employee under Chapter 5 at some earlier time`                               IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Service and absorption`

-- s 158(2): a soldier is insured for one year from the day of release from regular service under the
-- Security Service Law, other than service under a career commitment.
-- s 158(3): a volunteer in national service or community volunteering, or in civil-national service,
-- is insured for one year from the end of the service, if the service lasted long enough. Two texts of
-- (3) stand in the consolidation: the permanent text, which measures the service against the period a
-- female conscript serves under s 16(1) of the Security Service Law (not deposited), and the temporary
-- provision, which applies to one who began before 31 August 2026 and says 24 months (fork C1).
-- `a woman who served at least six months and married within 30 days of the day she stopped`: the
-- proviso of (3), which deems the full period served and counts the year from the day she stopped.
-- src:1445 | (2) חייל ששירת שירות סדיר על פי חוק שירות בטחון, למעט שירות צבאי לפי התחייבות לשירות קבע, מיום שחרורו מהשירות ולמשך שנה מאותו יום (להלן – חייל);
-- src:1446 | (3) [note: (הנוסח הקבוע):] מי ששירת כמתנדב בשירות לאומי או בהתנדבות קהילתית תקופה שאינה קצרה מתקופה שבה חייבת יוצאת צבא אשה בשירות סדיר על פי סעיף 16(1) לחוק שירות בטחון, מיום תום השירות ולמשך שנה מאותו יום; ואולם בת ששירתה כמתנדבת בשירות לאומי או בהתנדבות קהילתית, ותקופת שירותה בפועל לא פחתה משישה חודשים, והיא נישאה בתוך 30 הימים מהיום שבו הפסיקה בפועל את השירות הלאומי או ההתנדבות הקהילתית (להלן – יום הפסקת השירות), יראוה כמי ששירתה כמתנדבת בשירות לאומי או בהתנדבות קהילתית תקופה שאינה קצרה מתקופה שבה חייבת יוצאת צבא בשירות סדיר כאמור, ומנין השנה האמורה יחושב מיום הפסקת השירות;
-- src:1447 | [note: (הוראת שעה עד מועד הפקיעה של חוק שירות לאומי–אזרחי, התשע״ד–2014, ביום 31.8.2026, חלה גם על מי שהתחיל את שירותו לפני המועד האמור גם אחרי המועד האמור עד שייסים את שירותו):] מי ששירת כמתנדב בשירות לאומי או בהתנדבות קהילתית או כמשרת בשירות לאומי–אזרחי תקופה שאינה קצרה מ־24 חודשים, מיום תום השירות ולמשך שנה מאותו יום; ואולם בת ששירתה כמתנדבת בשירות לאומי או בהתנדבות קהילתית, ותקופת שירותה בפועל לא פחתה משישה חודשים, והיא נישאה בתוך 30 הימים מהיום שבו הפסיקה בפועל את השירות הלאומי או ההתנדבות הקהילתית (להלן – יום הפסקת השירות), יראוה כמי ששירתה כמתנדבת בשירות לאומי או בהתנדבות קהילתית תקופה שאינה קצרה מ־24 החודשים האמורים, ומנין השנה האמורה יחושב מיום הפסקת השירות;
DECLARE `A completed service` HAS
    `the day the service ended`                                                              IS A DATE
    `the months served`                                                                      IS A NUMBER
    `civil-national service`                                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the service began before 31 August 2026`                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `a woman who served at least six months and married within 30 days of the day she stopped` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 223 "מבוטח" (4): an immigrant, or a resident holding a permanent-residence visa and licence or an
-- A/5 temporary visa and licence under the Entry to Israel Law, who was given an absorption basket by
-- the Ministry of Aliyah and Integration, if not insured under Chapter 11.
-- src:2178 | (4) תושב ישראל שעלה לפי חוק השבות, או תושב ישראל שבידו אשרה ורישיון לישיבת קבע או אשרה ורישיון לישיבת ארעי מסוג א/5, לפי חוק הכניסה לישראל, שניתן לו סל קליטה מהמשרד לקליטת העליה, והכל אם אינם מבוטחים בביטוח אזרחים ותיקים וביטוח שאירים;
DECLARE `The absorption facts of a person` HAS
    `immigrated under the Law of Return`                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a permanent-residence visa and licence, or an A/5 temporary visa and licence`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `was given an absorption basket by the Ministry of Aliyah and Integration`                           IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 243: the Minister may fix classes who are not insured under Chapter 11 despite s 240; the
-- Institute may, if asked, insure one of them or end an insurance, on the terms fixed. The regulations
-- are not deposited (fork C2).
-- s 246(a): `the qualifying period ... has been completed`, which s 240(b) reads for a woman.
-- src:2449 | השר רשאי לקבוע סוגי בני אדם שעל אף הוראות סעיף 240 לא יהיו מבוטחים לפי פרק זה; ואולם המוסד רשאי, אם נתבקש לעשות כן, לבטח אדם מאלה או להפסיק ביטוחו לפי תנאים שנקבעו.
-- src:2440 | (ב) מבוטחת שאינה פטורה מתקופת אכשרה לפי סעיף 246(ב), ואשר לא נתמלאה לגביה כעובדת מבוטחת תקופת אכשרה המזכה לקצבת אזרח ותיק לפי סעיף 246(א), תהיה מבוטחת לענין פרק זה לפי סימן ג׳ בלבד.
DECLARE `The Chapter 11 facts of a person` HAS
    `of a class the Minister has excluded from insurance under section 243`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `insured at the person's own request under the regulations under section 243`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `has completed the qualifying period of section 246(a) as an insured employee`                  IS A BOOLEAN

-- The person. `name` identifies; two records with one name are one person.
DECLARE `A person for the statuses of the Law` HAS
    `name`                    IS A STRING
    `date of birth`           IS A DATE
    `sex`                     IS A `Sex`
    `residence`               IS A `The residence facts of a person`
    `work`                    IS A `The work facts of a person`
    `released from regular service` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `completed national or community service` IS A MAYBE `A completed service`
    `absorption`              IS A `The absorption facts of a person`
    `Chapter 11`              IS A `The Chapter 11 facts of a person`

§§ `Marriage, widowhood and the housewife (s 238)`

-- s 238 "עקרת בית": "אשה נשואה", a married woman. s 1 "אשתו" includes a woman "known in public as his
-- wife" who lives with him, but s 238 says "נשואה" (married), not "אשתו": whether the wider word
-- reaches her is fork H1.
-- src:2428 | ”עקרת בית“ – אשה נשואה, למעט עגונה, שבן זוגה מבוטח לפי פרק זה, שאינה עובדת ואינה עובדת עצמאית, ובכלל זה אישה כאמור שהיא חברת קיבוץ מתחדש;
-- src:129 | ”אשתו“ – לרבות הידועה בציבור כאשתו והיא גרה עמו;
DECLARE `Marital status` IS ONE OF
    `never married`
    `married`
    `divorced`
    `widowed`
    `known in public as the wife of a man and living with him, without being married to him`

-- s 1 "עגונה": a married woman whose spouse's traces have vanished for two years, including a woman
-- whose spouse has been abroad, without her consent, for such a period and has not supported her then.
-- src:203 | ”עגונה“ – אשה נשואה שזה שנתיים נעלמו עקבות בן זוגה, לרבות אשה שבן זוגה נמצא, שלא בהסכמתה, תקופה כאמור בחוץ לארץ ולא נשא באותו זמן במזונותיה;
DECLARE `A woman's marriage` HAS
    `marital status`                                                                                   IS A `Marital status`
    `her spouse's traces have vanished for two years`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `her spouse has been abroad for two years without her consent and has not supported her in that time` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 238 "אלמנה": the wife of the insured at his death, but not (1) one who was his wife for less than
-- a year (less than half a year, if she was 55 or over) and did not bear him a child, or (2) one who
-- in the five years before his death was separated from him for three years or more, including the
-- twelve months before the death, and was not entitled to maintenance from him by a judgment or a
-- written agreement, or he did not in fact bear her maintenance in the twelve months before his death;
-- (2) does not apply to a woman for whom a dependants' supplement was paid at the death under s 200
-- or 244.
-- src:2403 | ”אלמנה“ – מי שהיתה אשתו של המבוטח בשעת פטירתו, להוציא –
-- src:2404 | (1) מי שהיתה אשתו פחות משנה, ואם היא בת 55 שנים ומעלה – פחות מחצי שנה, ולא ילדה לו ילד;
-- src:2405 | (2) מי שבחמש השנים האחרונות שלפני פטירת המבוטח היתה נפרדת ממנו שלוש שנים לפחות ובכללן 12 חודשים שלפני פטירת המבוטח ולא היתה זכאית למזונות ממנו על פי פסק דין של בית משפט או בית דין מוסמך או על פי הסכם בכתב, או שהמבוטח לא נשא למעשה במזונותיה תוך 12 החודשים שלפני פטירתו; פסקה זו לא תחול על אשה שבעת פטירתו של המבוטח שולמה בעדה תוספת תלויים לפי סעיפים 200 או 244;
DECLARE `A widowing` HAS
    `she was his wife at his death`                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day of the marriage`                                                                        IS A DATE
    `the day of his death`                                                                           IS A DATE
    `she bore him a child`                                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the five years before his death she was separated from him for three years or more, including the twelve months before his death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `she was entitled to maintenance from him by a judgment or a written agreement`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `he did in fact bear her maintenance in the twelve months before his death`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `a dependants' supplement was paid for her at his death under section 200 or 244`                IS A BOOLEAN

-- The two readings of the last limb of paragraph (2) of "אלמנה" (fork W1): "ולא היתה זכאית למזונות ...
-- או שהמבוטח לא נשא למעשה במזונותיה" can be read as one alternative inside the condition of
-- separation, or as a second alternative to the whole condition.
DECLARE `A reading of the maintenance limb of paragraph (2) of the definition of a widow` IS ONE OF
    `the maintenance limbs are alternatives inside the condition of separation`
    `the lack of actual maintenance is an alternative to the whole of the separation condition`
    `the grammar of the maintenance limb is declined where the two readings differ`

-- s 238 "אלמנה בת קצבה": a widow who is not an employee or self-employed and is entitled to a pension
-- under s 132(1) to (5) or s 252. Entitlement to those pensions is a fact the Institute records
-- (ss 132 and 252 are not encoded; NOTES.md).
-- src:2429 | ”אלמנה בת קצבה“ – אלמנה שאינה עובדת ואינה עובדת עצמאית הזכאית לקצבה לפי סעיף 132(1) עד (5) או לפי סעיף 252;
DECLARE `A widow's pension fact` HAS
    `entitled to a pension under section 132(1) to (5) or section 252`                               IS A BOOLEAN

-- The two readings of "אשה נשואה" in "עקרת בית" for a woman known in public as a wife (fork H1).
DECLARE `A reading of the word married in the definition of a housewife` IS ONE OF
    `married means married only`
    `married includes a woman known in public as the wife and living with him`
    `the word married is declined for a woman known in public as the wife`

§§ `Two readings of residence`

-- s 2A speaks of "תושב ישראל"; s 65(a) "מבוטח" (2) of "יחיד היושב בישראל". Whether the second is the
-- first (so that s 2A's exclusions apply to it) the text does not say (fork R3).
DECLARE `A reading of the words sits in Israel in section 65(a)` IS ONE OF
    `sits in Israel is residence within section 2A`
    `sits in Israel is a matter of fact, whatever section 2A says`
    `the words sit in Israel are declined where section 2A would exclude a person who in fact lives in Israel`

-- How a day count that equals 183 exactly is read in s 2A(b)(4) and (c): the limbs speak of fewer than
-- 183 and of more than 183 (fork R4).
DECLARE `A reading of exactly 183 days in section 2A` IS ONE OF
    `183 days is counted with fewer than 183 days`
    `183 days is counted with more than 183 days`
    `183 days falls under neither limb, as the words read`
    `exactly 183 days is declined where the readings differ`

§§ `Where the day an age is reached does not exist`

-- A person reaches an age in months on the day that many months after the date of birth. Where the
-- later month lacks that day of the month (born on the 31st, reaching the age in a 30-day month; born
-- on 29 February, reaching it in a common year) the text does not say which day it is: the same
-- ambiguity as row IL-08's fork N4 (inventory item DATE). RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG): declined
-- by default; the other two readings kept by name. A day that exists is the same under all three.
DECLARE `A reading of the day an age is reached where the later month lacks the day of birth` IS ONE OF
    `age: the last day of the shorter month`
    `age: the 1st of the next month`
    `age: such a day is declined`

§§ `Sections 69, 69A and 71`

-- s 69(a): to the mother; but to the father if the child is with the father only and he is entitled.
-- The parents of a child as s 69 sees them: a mother and a father, or not (fork P1: two parents of one
-- sex, or none, are not in the words of the section).
-- src:837 | (א) קצבת ילדים תשולם לאם, אולם אם הילד נמצא עם האב בלבד, והאב זכאי לקצבה, תשולם הקצבה לאב.
DECLARE `The parents of a child, for section 69` IS ONE OF
    `a mother and a father`
    `a mother only`
    `a father only`
    `two parents of one sex`
    `no parent`

-- s 69(d): the Institute may, if the child's welfare requires it, pay a second parent who is not
-- entitled, or the guardian, or the person appointed under s 304(a). A decision of the Institute.
-- src:840 | (ד) גם אם נתמלאו התנאים של סעיף קטן (א) רשאי המוסד, אם טובת הילד מחייבת זאת, לשלם את הקצבה להורה שני שאינו בר־הקצבה, או לאפוטרופוס או למי שנתמנה לכך לפי סעיף 304(א).
DECLARE `A decision of the Institute under section 69(d)` IS ONE OF
    `to pay a second parent who is not entitled`
    `to pay the guardian`
    `to pay the person appointed under section 304(a)`

DECLARE `The facts of section 69` HAS
    `the parents`                                                                                    IS A `The parents of a child, for section 69`
    `the child is with the father only`                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the father is entitled to the allowance`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parent paid under section 69(a) asked that the allowance be paid to the other parent`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `a guardian was lawfully appointed`                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `a person was appointed under section 304(a)`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Institute's decision under section 69(d)`                                                   IS A MAYBE `A decision of the Institute under section 69(d)`

-- s 69(b) says the Institute SHALL pay the other parent when the parent paid under (a) asks it; s 69(d)
-- says the Institute MAY, if the child's welfare requires, pay someone else. Where a request under (b) and
-- a decision under (d) are both in the case, the text does not say which prevails (fork P2).
DECLARE `A reading of a request under section 69(b) and a decision under section 69(d) in one case` IS ONE OF
    `the request under section 69(b) prevails`
    `the decision under section 69(d) prevails`
    `declined where the two differ`

DECLARE `The person to whom the child allowance is paid` IS ONE OF
    `the mother`
    `the father`
    `the other parent, at the request of the parent paid under section 69(a)`
    `the guardian lawfully appointed`
    `the person appointed under section 304(a)`
    `a second parent who is not entitled, by decision of the Institute`

-- s 69A: a man whose children are by several women. A child in his count.
-- src:843 | על אף האמור בכל מקום אחר בסימן זה, היו למבוטח ילדים ממספר נשים יחולו לגביו הוראות אלה:
-- src:844 | (1) היה לו ילד כאמור בסעיף 68(ב), יבואו הילדים במניין כל אחת מהנשים בנפרד;
-- src:845 | (2) לא היה לו ילד כאמור בסעיף 68(ב), יבואו הילדים במניין האב; הוכיחה האם, להנחת דעתו של המוסד, כי אינה מקיימת משק בית משותף עם האב, וכי הילד לא סמוך על שולחנו של האב – יבוא הילד במניין האם.
DECLARE `A child of a man with children by several women` HAS
    `name`                                                                                                    IS A STRING
    `date of birth`                                                                                           IS A DATE
    `the name of the child's mother`                                                                          IS A STRING
    `the mother proved to the Institute's satisfaction that she keeps no joint household with the father and that the child does not depend on his table` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Whose count the child comes in under s 69A.
DECLARE `The count in which a child comes under section 69A` IS ONE OF
    `the count of its mother`
    `the count of the father`

-- The two readings of "ילד כאמור בסעיף 68(ב)" in s 69A(1): a child born before 1 June 2003 who is the
-- fourth or later "in the count of the parent's children". Whose count measures that, when s 69A is
-- itself what decides the counts, the text does not say (fork A1).
DECLARE `A reading of a child as in section 68(b), for section 69A(1)` IS ONE OF
    `measured in the count of all the man's children`
    `measured in the count of each woman's children`
    `declined where the two readings differ`

-- s 71: when the insured parent died or ceased to be insured.
-- src:851 | מת ההורה המבוטח או חדל להיות מבוטח, תשתלם מכוחו קצבת הילדים שהיתה משתלמת בעד הילד אילולא מת או אילולא חדל להיות מבוטח; ואולם אם היה לילד הורה שני, והוא זכאי לקצבה תשולם הקצבה מכוחו של ההורה השני.
DECLARE `The facts of section 71` HAS
    `the name of the parent who died or ceased to be insured`                                        IS A STRING
    `that parent is the child's father`                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day he or she died or ceased to be insured`                                                IS A DATE
    `the name of the child's second parent`                                                         IS A MAYBE STRING
    `the second parent is entitled to the child allowance`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the second parent also died or ceased to be insured`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the second parent died or ceased to be insured`                                         IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the child is with the mother only`                                                              IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `By virtue of whom the child allowance is paid under section 71` IS ONE OF
    `by virtue of the parent who died or ceased to be insured`
    `by virtue of the second parent`

-- When both parents died or ceased to be insured, s 71 does not say by virtue of which the allowance
-- is paid (fork S1).
DECLARE `A reading of section 71 where both parents died or ceased to be insured` IS ONE OF
    `by virtue of the parent s 67(b) would choose if both were alive and insured`
    `by virtue of the parent who died or ceased to be insured first`
    `section 71 is declined where the readings differ`

§§ `Rounding (s 381 and the Rounding Regulations 5746-1985)`

-- The Regulations round by the KIND of amount: a daily benefit computed on income to the agora (reg 2); a
-- cash benefit, which reg 3 says includes the child allowance for each child, to
-- the whole new shekel; a monthly income used as a base, and an amount that fixes entitlement or rate, to
-- the whole new shekel (reg 4); an amount collected from a person liable for maintenance (reg 5); an amount
-- used for charging insurance contributions (reg 6); and an addition, fine or overpayment ending in less
-- than a shekel, down (reg 7). The Regulations were made under the 1968 consolidation of the Law and cite
-- its section numbers; the kinds are named here by what the Regulations describe.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/regulations/national-insurance-rules-for-rounding-amounts-regulations-5746-1985.he.wiki.txt
DECLARE `A kind of amount, for the Rounding Regulations` IS ONE OF
    `a daily benefit, or another daily payment of the Institute, computed on income, regulation 2`
    `a cash benefit, including a child allowance for each child and a dependants' supplement, regulation 3`
    `a monthly income used as the base of a benefit, or an amount that fixes entitlement to a payment or its rate, regulation 4`
    `an amount collected from a person liable for maintenance, regulation 5`
    `an amount used in charging insurance contributions, regulation 6`
    `an addition, a fine, an overpayment, ending in less than one new shekel, regulation 7`
    `a benefit under Chapter 8 of the Law (insolvency proceedings; the Regulations' Chapter 6C), which regulation 3 leaves out`

-- The allowance for one child before rounding: the amount s 68(a) or (b) gives, and the s 68(c) supplement
-- (0 where none is added). Row IL-06's `The allowance for a child in the count` carries the same two figures.
DECLARE `The allowance for one child, before rounding` HAS
    `the allowance under section 68(a) or (b)`            IS A NUMBER
    `the supplement under section 68(c)`                  IS A NUMBER

-- Regulation 3 rounds the child allowance for each child and the supplement for dependants. Whether the s 68(c) supplement,
-- which s 68(c) "adds to" the allowance for the third and fourth child, is rounded with the allowance as one
-- amount or on its own is not said (fork R5). RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG): declined by default,
-- and declined only where the two give different totals.
DECLARE `A reading of the child allowance and the supplement of section 68(c), for rounding` IS ONE OF
    `the supplement is rounded with the allowance as one amount`
    `the supplement is rounded on its own`
    `rounding is declined where the two readings differ`

§§ `The updating clause of the basic amount (s 1 "הסכום הבסיסי")`

-- s 1 "הסכום הבסיסי" paragraph (2) fixes, for the child allowance, three amounts "denominated for 2015"
-- (150, 188, 140 new shekels), and the updating paragraph (3) updates them "from 2015 on, on 1 January of
-- each year, by the rate of rise of the index published last before that day compared with the index
-- published last before 1 January of the previous year", except that "on 1 January 2025 the amounts of
-- paragraph (2) will not be updated and will be in that year as they were on 1 January 2024".
-- The index is the consumer price index (s 1 "מדד"), the Central Bureau of Statistics' general index. The
-- Bureau publishes the index for November on about 15 December, so the index published last before a
-- 1 January is the November index. The Bureau changes the base of the index; to compare two readings in
-- two bases the later reading is expressed in the earlier base by the Bureau's linkage coefficient. Those
-- numbers are data, not law, and live in nii-il33-published-figures.l4.
-- src:187 | (א) בעד הילד הראשון והחמישי ואילך במניין ילדיו של ההורה – 150 שקלים חדשים [note: (נקוב לשנת 2015; בשנים 2024–2025, 169 ש״ח; בשנת 2026, 173 ש״ח)];
-- src:188 | (ב) בעד הילד השני, השלישי והרביעי שבמניין ילדיו של ההורה – 188 שקלים חדשים [note: (נקוב לשנת 2015; בשנים 2024–2025, 214 ש״ח; בשנת 2026, 219 ש״ח)];
-- src:189 | (ג) על אף האמור בפסקאות משנה (א) ו־(ב), לעניין גמלה לפי חוק הבטחת הכנסה, או תוספת כאמור בסעיף 68(ג) – 140 שקלים חדשים [note: (נקוב לשנת 2015; בשנים 2024–2025, 158 ש״ח; בשנת 2026, 162 ש״ח)];
-- src:196 | (2) לעניין כל גמלה למעט קצבת ילדים המשתלמת לפי הוראות סימן ב׳ בפרק ד׳ – משנת 2007 ואילך – ב־1 בינואר של כל שנה, לפי שיעור עליית המדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני אותו יום לעומת המדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני יום 1 בינואר של השנה הקודמת;
-- src:197 | (3) לעניין קצבת ילדים המשתלמת לפי הוראות סימן ב׳ בפרק ד׳ – משנת 2015 ואילך – ב־1 בינואר של כל שנה, לפי שיעור עליית המדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני אותו יום לעומת המדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני יום 1 בינואר של השנה הקודמת ואולם, ב־1 בינואר של שנת 2025 לא יתעדכנו הסכומים הקבועים בפסקה (2) לרישה של הגדרה זו, והם יהיו באותה שנה כפי שהיו ביום כ׳ בטבת התשפ״ד (1 בינואר 2024);
DECLARE `The index readings for the update of a 1 January` HAS
    `the index last published before that 1 January, in the base of the earlier reading`  IS A NUMBER
    `the index last published before the previous 1 January`                              IS A NUMBER
    `the twelve-month change the CBS published with the later reading, in percent`        IS A NUMBER

-- When the index published last before the day is LOWER than the one before: there is then no "rise" (עלייה)
-- of the index. Whether the clause then leaves the basic amount as it was, or lowers it by the fall, the
-- text does not say (fork U1). RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG): declined by default, and declined only
-- where the two give different amounts.
DECLARE `A reading of a fall in the index, in the updating clause of the basic amount` IS ONE OF
    `a fall in the index leaves the basic amount unchanged`
    `a fall in the index lowers the basic amount by the fall`
    `a fall in the index is declined where the two readings differ`

-- The three amounts of paragraph (2), computed by the updating clause for a 1 January.
DECLARE `The basic amounts of section 1 paragraph (2), computed by the updating clause` HAS
    `under paragraph (2)(a)`  IS A NUMBER
    `under paragraph (2)(b)`  IS A NUMBER
    `under paragraph (2)(c)`  IS A NUMBER

§§ `The Income Support Law, 5741-1980 (the gate: whether a benefit is paid for a month)`

-- Source: ../../../income-support-law-5741-1980/registers/source-bundle/income-support-law-5741-1980.he.wiki.txt
-- (Hebrew Wikisource raw wikitext, sha256 91649d29...bca1a7). A `src:N` comment under the Income Support
-- Law's modules quotes line N of THAT file.
--
-- s 68(c) of the National Insurance Law reads whether a parent is paid "גמלה לפי חוק הבטחת הכנסה" (a benefit
-- under the Income Support Law) for a month. This row encodes the Law's gate, ss 2 to 4, 5(b), 7(b), 8, 14(a)
-- and 14A(a): who is entitled, and when what is computed is paid. The grounds of s 2(a)(1) to (9) that the
-- Law leaves to regulations or to an authority's determination, the rates of the Second Schedule, and the
-- income of Chapter 4 (ss 9 to 12) are inputs of the case, or are not encoded (NOTES.md).
-- The grounds of s 2(a): (4), reaching the retirement age, is derived; (6) is repealed; (2A) is a separate
-- flag; the rest are the case's, each as the Law words it.
DECLARE `A ground of entitlement under section 2(a) of the Income Support Law` IS ONE OF
    `unable to work and earn a living, or not placeable in any work, as determined under regulations, section 2(a)(1)`
    `registered at the employment service as unemployed and offered no suitable work, section 2(a)(2)`
    `working or in training with income below the income that bars payment, section 2(a)(3)`
    `a parent of a child in his keeping, with him and not yet two, section 2(a)(5)`
    `devoting his main time to the care of a sick spouse or child who needs constant supervision, section 2(a)(7)`
    `performing community-service work under the Penal Law, section 2(a)(8)`
    `staying in a shelter for battered women for more than 30 days, section 2(a)(9)`

DECLARE `The facts of a claimant under the Income Support Law` HAS
    `grounds under section 2(a)(1), (2), (3), (5), (7), (8) and (9) that hold`                IS A LIST OF `A ground of entitlement under section 2(a) of the Income Support Law`
    `a ground of the First Schedule under section 2(a)(2A) holds`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `a resident of Israel in the Area within section 378 of the Insurance Law`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `was a resident of Israel for the 24 consecutive months before the claim`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `receives a pension under Chapter 5 or Chapter 11 of the Insurance Law`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `is in an institution maintained wholly at the expense of the State or another named body, section 3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `serves regular service in the Israel Defense Forces, or is the wife of one who does, section 3(2)`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a member of a corporation responsible for the livelihood of its members, section 3(3)`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a student at an institution the Minister fixed, and not within the exceptions of section 3(4)(a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is barred by section 3C (a conviction for a terror offence)`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `stayed outside Israel on every day of the month, section 14A(a)`                         IS A BOOLEAN

-- A claimant with the facts the Law asks about: the person is the Insurance Law's person (residence, birth).
DECLARE `A claimant under the Income Support Law` HAS
    `the person`  IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
    `the facts`   IS A `The facts of a claimant under the Income Support Law`

DECLARE `The money of a month under the Income Support Law` HAS
    `the benefit for a person without income, from the Second Schedule`                       IS A NUMBER
    `the income, computed under sections 9 to 12`                                             IS A NUMBER
    `the determining sum that applies to the claimant under section 7(a), if regulations fix one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the first day of the month in which the claim was submitted`                              IS A DATE

§§ `The Maintenance (Assurance of Payment) Law, 5732-1972 (the gate: whether a payment is made for a month)`

-- Source: ../../../maintenance-assurance-of-payment-law-5732-1972/registers/source-bundle/maintenance-assurance-of-payment-law-5732-1972.he.wiki.txt
-- (Hebrew Wikisource raw wikitext, sha256 0607398d...e8d7). A `src:N` comment under the Maintenance Law's module
-- quotes line N of THAT file.
-- s 68(c) of the National Insurance Law reads whether a parent is paid "תשלום חודשי לפי חוק המזונות (הבטחת
-- תשלום)" for a month. This row encodes the Law's gate: who is a creditor (s 1), s 2(a) entitlement, s 3 the
-- rate, s 6(a) the period, s 9 enforcement, s 9A absences abroad. The rates in regulations (s 3, s 20), the
-- Minister of Justice's exceptions (s 9(d), s 9A(c)(2)) and the exemptions of s 9A(c) and (d) are inputs.
DECLARE `The facts of a maintenance creditor` HAS
    `a maintenance judgment was given in the person's favour`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a maintenance judgment was given in favour of the person's minor child in the person's keeping` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lives with the debtor`                                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `a resident of Israel in the Area within section 378 of the Insurance Law`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the debtor was an Israeli resident on the day of the judgment`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the debtor was an Israeli resident for at least 24 of the 48 months before the day of the judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is pursuing enforcement proceedings on the judgment`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister of Justice's regulations let payment continue despite enforcement, section 9(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day from which the judgment orders maintenance`                                       IS A DATE
    `the day to which the judgment orders maintenance, if it names one`                        IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the day the request for payment was submitted to the Institute`                           IS A DATE
    `the monthly maintenance the judgment orders`                                              IS A NUMBER
    `the monthly rate the regulations fix, if they are given`                                  IS A MAYBE NUMBER

-- s 9A(b): a creditor who leaves Israel. (1) four or more departures in a calendar year: nothing for the month
-- of the departure and the month of the return and a month wholly abroad, from the fourth departure on; (2)
-- fewer than four departures but more than 72 days abroad in the calendar year: nothing for each month in
-- which the stay abroad exceeded those 72 days. (c) and (d): exemptions and the 183-day rule are inputs.
DECLARE `The absences of a maintenance creditor in a month` HAS
    `departures from Israel in the calendar year, up to and including the month`              IS A NUMBER
    `the month contains a departure after the third, a return after the third, or only days abroad` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days abroad in the calendar year, up to the end of the month`                            IS A NUMBER
    `days abroad in the month`                                                                IS A NUMBER
    `exempt under section 9A(c)`                                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `treated as outside Israel under section 9A(d)`                                           IS A BOOLEAN

-- A month in which the period of payment begins or ends partway (s 6(a)): the Law pays monthly and does not say how
-- such a month is paid (fork M1). RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG).
DECLARE `A reading of a month in which the period of payment begins or ends partway` IS ONE OF
    `a month in which the period begins or ends partway is paid in full`
    `a month in which the period begins or ends partway is not paid`
    `a month in which the period begins or ends partway is declined where the two readings differ`

§§ `A self-employed person who works outside Israel (s 75(a)(2))`

-- s 75(a)(2) insures "עובד עצמאי" (a self-employed person) without a word about where he works. s 76,
-- which limits insurance abroad, speaks only of "העובד" (the worker, an employee). Whether the
-- insurance of a self-employed person reaches work done outside Israel the text does not say (fork C3).
-- src:946 | (2) עובד עצמאי, למעט מי שנמנה עם סוג אנשים שהוצאו מכלל עובדים עצמאיים, לענין סעיף זה, בתקנות ולאחר התייעצות עם ועדת העבודה והרווחה;
-- src:956 | (א) העובד בחוץ לארץ מבוטח לפי פרק זה אם הוא ומעבידו הם תושבי ישראל וחוזה העבודה נקשר בישראל, או אף אם חוזה העבודה לא נקשר בישראל ובמקום העבודה אין ביטוח נפגעי עבודה חובה לפי החוק ונמסרה הודעה על קיומו של החוזה כפי שנקבע בתקנות.
DECLARE `A reading of a self-employed person who works outside Israel, under section 75(a)(2)` IS ONE OF
    `insured wherever the work is done`
    `insured only if the work is done in Israel`
    `declined where the two readings differ`

§§ `Two further forks (version 0.1.2, from the independent pass)`

-- s 223 "מבוטח" (4): "תושב ישראל שעלה לפי חוק השבות, או תושב ישראל שבידו אשרה ורישיון לישיבת קבע או אשרה ורישיון לישיבת
-- ארעי מסוג א/5 ... שניתן לו סל קליטה מהמשרד לקליטת העליה": does "who was given an absorption basket" qualify both the
-- immigrant and the visa holder, or only the visa holder? Both are grammatical (fork L1). It matters only for a person not
-- insured under Chapter 11 (a person insured under it is insured for long-term care by (1)).
-- src:2178 | (4) תושב ישראל שעלה לפי חוק השבות, או תושב ישראל שבידו אשרה ורישיון לישיבת קבע או אשרה ורישיון לישיבת ארעי מסוג א/5, לפי חוק הכניסה לישראל, שניתן לו סל קליטה מהמשרד לקליטת העליה, והכל אם אינם מבוטחים בביטוח אזרחים ותיקים וביטוח שאירים;
DECLARE `A reading of the absorption basket in section 223 "insured" (4)` IS ONE OF
    `the absorption basket qualifies both the immigrant and the visa holder`
    `the absorption basket qualifies only the visa holder`
    `the absorption basket is declined where the two readings differ`

-- s 69(a): "קצבת ילדים תשולם לאם" (the allowance shall be paid to the mother). Whether the mother is paid when she is
-- not herself entitled to the allowance (the father being the insured parent) the text does not say (fork P3,
-- revised in 0.1.2). Reading 1: she is paid. Reading 2: (a) pays an entitled mother; where the mother is not
-- entitled and the father is, the father is paid.
-- src:837 | (א) קצבת ילדים תשולם לאם, אולם אם הילד נמצא עם האב בלבד, והאב זכאי לקצבה, תשולם הקצבה לאב.
DECLARE `A reading of the payee where the mother is not entitled, section 69(a)` IS ONE OF
    `the mother is paid whether or not she is entitled`
    `the mother is paid only if she is entitled; otherwise an entitled father is paid`
    `the payee is declined where the two readings differ`

§§ `The readings this row takes`

-- Every fork of this row is a switch whose default is a refusal (Meng, SHRUG, 2026-10-08). The switches
-- of the rules in this row travel together in one record; `the readings this row takes` is the default
-- (everything declined where the readings differ) and each field has a setter in the rules modules that
-- own it. A reading is an argument, never a field of the case records.
DECLARE `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide` HAS
    `the day an age is reached`                              IS A `A reading of the day an age is reached where the later month lacks the day of birth`
    `exactly 183 days in section 2A`                         IS A `A reading of exactly 183 days in section 2A`
    `the words sits in Israel in section 65(a)`              IS A `A reading of the words sits in Israel in section 65(a)`
    `a self-employed person who works outside Israel`        IS A `A reading of a self-employed person who works outside Israel, under section 75(a)(2)`
    `the word married in the definition of a housewife`      IS A `A reading of the word married in the definition of a housewife`
    `the maintenance limb of the definition of a widow`      IS A `A reading of the maintenance limb of paragraph (2) of the definition of a widow`
    `section 71 where both parents died or ceased to be insured` IS A `A reading of section 71 where both parents died or ceased to be insured`
    `a request under section 69(b) and a decision under section 69(d)` IS A `A reading of a request under section 69(b) and a decision under section 69(d) in one case`
    `a fall in the index, in the updating clause of the basic amount` IS A `A reading of a fall in the index, in the updating clause of the basic amount`
    `a month in which the period of payment begins or ends partway`        IS A `A reading of a month in which the period of payment begins or ends partway`
    `the child allowance and the supplement of section 68(c), for rounding` IS A `A reading of the child allowance and the supplement of section 68(c), for rounding`
    `the absorption basket in section 223 "insured" (4)`     IS A `A reading of the absorption basket in section 223 "insured" (4)`
    `the payee where the mother is not entitled`             IS A `A reading of the payee where the mother is not entitled, section 69(a)`
    `a child as in section 68(b), for section 69A(1)`        IS A `A reading of a child as in section 68(b), for section 69A(1)`
